{title: Of the Father's Love Begotten}
{artist: Prudentius · tr. John Mason Neale}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 72}

Verse 1
[F]Of the Father's [Dm]love be[Bb]gotten [C]ere the worlds be[F]gan to be,
he is Alpha and O[Dm]mega, [Bb]he the [C]source, the ending [F]he —
of the things that [Bb]are, that [F]have been, and that [Bb]future [C]years shall [Dm]see,
[F]ever[C]more and [F]evermore.

Verse 2
[F]At His Word [Dm]they were [C]created; He commanded; it was done:
Heav'n and earth and depths [Bb]of [C]ocean In their [F]threefold order
one; All that grows [Bb]beneath the [F]shining Of the [Bb]moon [C]and burning [Dm]sun,
[F]Evermore and [F]evermore!

Verse 3
[F]He is found [Dm]in human [C]fashion, Death and sorrow here to
know, That the race of [Bb]Adam's [C]children, Doomed by [F]law to
endless woe, May not [Bb]henceforth die [F]and perish In [Bb]the [C]dreadful gulf [Dm]below,
[F]Evermore and [F]evermore!

Verse 4
[F]Oh that birth [Dm]forever blessèd! [C]When the virgin, full of
grace, By the Holy Ghost [Bb]conceiving, [C]Bare the Savior [F]of our
race; And the [Bb]Babe, the [F]world's Redeemer, First revealed [C]His sacred [Dm]face,
[F]Evermore and [F]evermore!

Verse 5
[F]O ye heights [Dm]of heav'n [C]adore Him; Angel hosts, His praises
sing; Pow'rs, dominions, bow before [Bb]Him, [C]and extol our [F]God and
King: Let no tongue [Bb]on earth [F]be silent, Every [Bb]voice [C]in concert [Dm]ring,
[F]Evermore and [F]evermore!
